WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
- Let's talk about "Teen Wolf: The Movie."

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.210
So does it pick up wherever
the series left off?

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.320
- No, it doesn't actually.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.910
So the series, it's 15
years after the series.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:09.743
- Okay.
- Which is wild

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.810
because my character was
always younger than Tyler.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.400
- Yeah.
- I was always playing younger

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.870
and now my character's older
than Tyler by like three years.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.090
- Yeah.
- Or two years

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.890
or something like that, so, no,

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.390
it's a completely different world.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.580
My character has moved
away from Beacon Hills

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.920
which is like where
the town is in our show

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.020
and he's in Los Angeles trying

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.180
to step out of the hero-ship role.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.890
- Yeah.
- Which he was the hero

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.350
and like the leader of
the pack back in the day.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.850
Now he's kind of trying to live life

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.640
as like a normal human, but
it doesn't work out so well.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.990
- I do think that's really cool though,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.280
when you take time in between

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.650
'cause then you have more
story to like uncover

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.790
from what's been happening in between.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.590
I think that's really clever.
- It is cool, yeah.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.260
One of our characters has
a son, a 15 year old boy.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.093
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:50.093 --> 00:00:50.926
- Which is-
- That happens,

00:00:50.926 --> 00:00:53.092
all of a sudden people grow
up and you're like, "I'm old."

00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:54.570
(Tyler laughs)
Yeah.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:55.403
No, that's crazy.

00:00:55.403 --> 00:00:56.670
That's cool that all the lives are, like,

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.222
completely different.
- Yeah.

00:00:58.222 --> 00:00:59.055
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:01.110
- I heard that you almost
played another wolf, right?

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.130
- I did, yeah.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.470
I was up against Taylor Lautner,

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.680
it was between he and I
for Jacob in "Twilight."

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.151
- That's huge!

00:01:09.151 --> 00:01:11.310
- It would've been huge
but I was really young.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.143
I was like 16.

00:01:12.143 --> 00:01:14.670
I wasn't ready for the type
of attention that he got.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:15.503
- Yeah.
- You know,

00:01:15.503 --> 00:01:16.410
so I had to wait a couple more years

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.340
and then-
- That's smart

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.480
'cause it is a lot of attention.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.313
- It was a lot.

00:01:19.313 --> 00:01:21.360
He got a lot at that age
and I commend him for it

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.220
but I don't know if I
was fully ready for it

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.350
which I owe the me not getting it,

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.273
you know?
- Yeah.

